"bm_george|All three came from brand-new customers with no past orders at all.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Each order is only a piece, small enough to stay under one shop\u2019s limit. Put the pieces together and they add up to one order for a recipe for a germ that makes people very sick.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|All three orders give the same reason, in exactly the same words: vaccine work.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|My screening desk is the first safeguard, but Boston has others too: lab signatures, warnings shared between shops, each shop\u2019s own check, wastewater testing across the city, and a hospital line that can make a new vaccine in about three weeks.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|What we can actually check":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
