"bm_george|A guess is not proof. I can tell you who I think sent these orders, but my guess alone is not enough to block a single order.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Blocking an order puts it back on the shelf. The shop keeps working, and the customer can appeal to a person.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|The machine at the screening desk can flag orders all night, which no person could do. But blocking an order can cost a lab a week of work, so people decide who is allowed to hold an order and who has to sign before an order is blocked.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
